# High-Level Changelog

- 2026-10-28T08:39:24+00:00 — Updated chat execution cards so child-agent calls are visually distinct from tool calls with a larger highlighted rectangle and explicit guidance text prompting users to click to view child-agent execution details.

- 2026-10-28T08:14:25+00:00 — Added context-selection loop resilience in the backend planner pipeline: the agent now tracks recently requested context windows, surfaces loop hints to planning prompts, blocks repeated looped window requests, and exits with a clear limit message instead of spinning indefinitely.

- 2026-10-28T07:36:05+00:00 — Updated backend trace, agent-session, and LLM log file naming so generated filenames now begin with a UTC timestamp prefix, making files sortable by creation time while preserving existing agent-based identifiers.

- 2026-10-28T05:20:36+00:00 — Documented current permitted and prohibited cross-layer dependencies and added a component/dependency diagram for the frontend, API, agent, persistence, learner, and external integrations.

- 2026-10-28T05:12:11+00:00 — Unified the agent execution limit across API, CLI, and child runs: `MAX_LOOPS` from backend settings is now the default when no user preference is saved, and execution-limit warnings report the effective value.

- 2026-10-27T16:46:03+00:00 — Completed child-run stability fixes so parent execution no longer fails when a child is still running at collection time: collection now remains in a running/pending state, retries cleanly, and preserves terminal child failures; also aligned child timeout runtime to the approved 10-minute window and tightened child-card/task UI behavior and context-memory prompt semantics.

- 2026-10-27T09:09:58+00:00 — Reduced backend startup latency by removing the unconditional full memory-index rebuild from API readiness; interrupted indexing work now resumes in the background, with startup-phase timing logs.

- 2026-10-27T07:30:00+00:00 — Integrated new-chat policy settings into the yellow New Chat control and added a form editor alongside the existing JSON editor.

- 2026-10-27T06:30:00+00:00 — Improved Armory sidebar layout so policy, tools, subagents, and MCP servers use full-width cards, while connected MCP server tools and resources are visible in their server card.

- 2026-10-27T00:00:00+00:00 — Redesigned Armory policy and catalog cards, added expandable tool/subagent/server details, and made Usage analytics refresh continuously during agent runs with clear cache labeling.

- 2026-10-27T06:23:13+00:00 — Made agent execution-limit stops fail cleanly with actionable guidance instead of emitting an unexpected-error traceback.

- 2026-10-27T06:26:04+00:00 — Redesigned the session Armory and Memory views for clearer navigation, readable content, stronger status summaries, search, and expandable details.

- 2026-10-26T11:40:00+00:00 — Fixed learner extraction crashing when a completed session used an MCP-backed tool.

- 2026-10-26T16:20:00+00:00 — Kept resource call names and IDs visible after live execution, and redesigned the session Usage tab for readable, fully padded metrics without horizontal overflow.

- 2026-10-26T11:10:00+00:00 — Improved authenticated MCP setup with a default `/auth/login` URL, agent user-ID prefilling, immediate connected-state display after registration, and reliable reconnect cleanup.

- 2026-10-26T09:40:00+00:00 — Fixed agent execution crashing when connected MCP tools were available to the planner.

- 2026-10-26T14:15:00+00:00 — Made MCP connection failures visible in an automatically expanded Connection Logs section while adding or editing a server, with exact backend validation messages.

- 2026-10-26T08:30:00+00:00 — Improved the MCP login setup form with clearly grouped credential and optional response-mapping fields, required-field markers, and explanatory guidance.

- 2026-10-26T12:00:00+00:00 — Added the approved execution plan for expanding the learner into a governed, decision-aware memory system covering user context, Armory and child-agent guidance, workflows, corrections, retrieval, promotion, documentation, and dedicated Graphify outputs.
- 2026-10-26T13:30:00+00:00 — Expanded the learner to capture seven governed memory types from conversation, Armory, and child-agent evidence, and deliver decision-aware advisory memory to both fast and planner decisions.
- 2026-10-26T15:00:00+00:00 — Hardened governed memory publication with chunk-level admin-promotion controls, deterministic privacy checks, terminal failure records, retention classes, and complete retrieval traces.

- 2026-10-26T08:20:00+00:00 — Added MCP server deletion controls and optional credentialed HTTP MCP connections that log in automatically, use bearer tokens, and refresh expired tokens once.

- 2026-10-22T06:50:40+00:00 — Added mandatory changelog process and tracking files in `/docuemtation` for all future codebase changes.
- 2026-10-22T07:08:27+00:00 — Centralized executor-output validation, deterministic sanitization, persistence, automatic context ingestion, trusted messages, and completion events in the output security gate.
- 2026-10-22T07:08:27+00:00 — Preserved direct context-memory selection while routing context-selection pause notes through the existing human-input and output-security flow before selection resumes.
- 2026-10-22T07:08:27+00:00 — Added focused regression coverage for output sanitization, memory commits, replay idempotency, bounded context ingestion, human output, and planned ordering.
- 2026-10-22T09:31:35+00:00 — Unified direct and planned actions behind one execution dispatcher and one result collector, removing the duplicate hidden planned-step execution path.
- 2026-10-22T09:31:35+00:00 — Simplified the graph so input security, result collection, output security, and context selection each have one fixed outgoing edge, with all routing decisions owned by the execution dispatcher.
